\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{\b Noted Tuesday, February 10, 2015\b0 , in Winnipeg, and posted on the Yahoo! Groups WordStar group:}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{WordStar recognizes an undocumented \u8220?.wi\u8221? dot command:}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{It\u8217?s a regular dot command, showing a \u8220?.\u8221? in the flag column, not a \u8220?1,\u8221? which indicates a dot command that works best at the top of a page, or a \u8220?:\u8221? for a merge-print dot command.  (And invalid dot commands show a \u8220??\u8221? \u8212? try \u8220?.wx\u8221? for instance; \u8220?.wi\u8221? is not invalid.)}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{My hope was that it was an undocumented \u8220?widow-orphan control\u8221? dot command, but it doesn\u8217?t seem to do anything.  I tried it on its own and with arguments of:}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .wi 0}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .wi 1}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .wi 2}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .wi off}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .wi on}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .wi dis }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{It\u8217?s recognized in WordStar for DOS 4.0 right through to WordStar 7.0.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{It\u8217?s not for character-width; that\u8217?s the \u8220?.cw\u8221? dot command.  And I doubt it stands for \u8220?WordStar International,\u8221? since, as I said, the command is recognized in WordStar 4.0, and the company was known as MicroPro International back then.}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{Anyone know what it\u8217?s for?  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{Rob}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{\page \b Noted Tuesday, November 9, 2021:\b0 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{In all of the WordStar program files, there is only one reference to \u8220?widow,\u8221? and that\u8217?s in WSHELP.OVR, but I can find no way to access that message from within a WordStar document.  There are zero referencs to \u8220?orphan.\u8221?}\par
